ething in return if you  think about it most Dividends are only  about five percent of what you put in  per year so if you put in a thousand  dollars you're only going to get fifty  dollars back you can't live off fifty  dollars you need a lot more to get a lot  more out in line with these dividends I  also do a little bit of Swing trading  that allows me to supplement those  dividends so I'll buy a share that I  know is a good dividend at paying share  but then at the same time it may go up  quite a lot and I'll be happy to sell it  and find something else for a better  price it's very simple buy load sell  High the tactic doesn't always work  hence why it is predominantly a dividend  portfolio and the swing trades just come  by basically luck the last two are very  obvious as an architect and anybody in  the architecture profession most of the  time you're going to have your own job  you're going to be actually working for  somebody or for yourself so that means  you're going to have a salary as the  base Foundation of your income for me  personally at the moment it is about a  60 40 split with a salary at 60 and this  side incomes at 40. the side incomes  have been growing very rapidly over the  past couple of years and hopefully it  will be able to destroy that 60 40 split  very very soon and last but not least  anybody in a position and working for a  good company may be offered some bonuses  that add to the streams of income that's  all for me today guys they are my 12  streams of income to decide you'll find  more great architectural content down  below you'll find the Subscribe button  and feel free to leave any comments down  below like I said that is it for me so  like always I'll see you next Monday
 

